{
  "id": "arousal_window_coreg",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "depends_on": [
    "affective_state_core"
  ],
  "self_load_only": true,
  "area": "retina",
  "description": "AROUSAL / WINDOW-OF-TOLERANCE with CO-REGULATION (block 239000). Instantiates Siegel's window of tolerance, Porges' polyvagal band, and the altricial co-regulation bond (Harlow, block 233000) as graph rules riding the REAL affective_state_core AffectiveState.arousal. A stressor pushes arousal; outside the tolerated band [lo,hi] fires a dysregulated state (hyper > hi, hypo < lo). A REGULATED caregiver present couples (leaky sd_blend pull) the infant's arousal toward the caregiver's, returning it to the window faster than self-regulation alone; a dysregulated / absent caregiver does not. Successful co-regulation WIDENS the window and raises the safety prior (development/healing); dysregulation without co-regulation NARROWS it and lowers the safety prior (trauma). 'Kids do well if they can' (Greene): dysregulation is a STATE to be regulated, never a badness -- NO reward/punishment anywhere. self_load_only, default-OFF; NO Rust, NO new Term.",
  "microtheory": {
    "name": "window_of_tolerance_coregulation",
    "description": "Arousal is tolerated within a band; outside it the agent is dysregulated. An external regulated caregiver entrains arousal back into the band (borrowed regulation); repeated co-regulation widens the band (internalisation); repeated unsupported stress narrows it."
  },
